<title>UK: Smithkline Infanrix Hepatitis approved in EU.</title>
<headline>Smithkline Infanrix Hepatitis approved in EU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based drugs group SmithKline Beecham Plc said on Monday that its Infanrix combination vaccine including protection against hepatitis B, had been approved in the European Union.</p>
<p>In a statement SmithKline said the vaccine would be the first to offer protection against Hepatitis B at the same time as diphtheria, tetanus and whooping cough.  </p>
<p>The company said hepatitis B was one of the most serious and frequent viral infections world-wide. The World Health Organisation has set a target for universal vaccination against the virus by the end of 1997.</p>
<p>The Infanrix paediatric vaccine without hepatitis B protection is already licensed in 25 countries including the U.S, Germany and Italy.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
